;; rust.tsg — placeholder stack-graphs rules for Rust.
;;
;; We ship this file so the `ResolverService` architectural seam
;; exists for Rust (plugins report `resolver_kind =
;; ResolverKind::StackGraphs`), and so a future contributor can
;; iteratively add real scope rules without touching the resolver
;; plumbing.
;;
;; The substantive work for Rust cross-file / cross-crate resolution
;; is done by the companion `cgg_resolve::cross_file` resolver, which
;; consumes the `use` / `pub use` / crate-root records emitted by the
;; extractor. That resolver already handles:
;;
;;   * `use a::b::c`                            (direct imports)
;;   * `use a::b::{X, Y as Z, self}`            (grouped imports)
;;   * `use a::b::c as d`                       (aliased imports)
;;   * `pub use a::b::c` chains (up to 8 deep)  (re-export chains)
;;   * cross-crate calls keyed on Cargo package names
;;   * full-path calls like `a::b::c()`         (receiver-hint driven)
;;
;; What a serious `rust.tsg` would still need to add: `impl` blocks,
;; trait dispatch, method calls with receiver-type inference,
;; generics/lifetimes, and macro expansion. That is on the order of a
;; multi-thousand-line file comparable to
;; `tree-sitter-stack-graphs-python`; it is deferred to v2.
;;
;; For now the only thing this file promises is that the grammar
;; compiles and a StackGraph can be built without errors.

(source_file) @_root {
}
